ymmetric convex bodies in $\\R^n$ invariant under $n-2$ orthogonal hyperplanes reflections, we establish the logarithmic Brunn--Minkowski inequality and classify all equality cases without regularity assumptions. We derive the logarithmic Minkowski inequality and rigidity for cone-volume measures, including an explicit classification for bodies of revolution and uniqueness for simplicial polytopes in the prescribed symmetry class.\nL17: Subjects:  | Metric Geometry (math.MG); Analysis of PDEs (math.AP); Differential Geometry (math.DG)\nL18: Cite as:  | cite9†arXiv:2608.20730 [math.MG]\nL19:    | (or cite10†arXiv:2608.20730v3 [math.MG] for this version)\nL20:    | cite11†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2608.20730†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL21: ## Submission history\nL22: \nL23: From: XiaoRui Lu [cite12†view email ]\nL24: cite5†[v1] Fri, 21 Aug 2026 04:22:15 UTC (21 KB)\nL25: cite13†[v2] Thu, 27 Aug 2026 05:57:39 UTC (21 KB)\nL26: [v3] Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:10:21 UTC (20 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled Logarithmic Brunn--Minkowski Inequality under $n-2$ Reflection Symmetries, by XiaoRui Lu\nL33: \nL34:   * cite7†View PDF L35:   * cite8†HTML (experimental) L36:   * cite14†TeX Source L37: \nL38: cite15†view license†creativecommons.org L39: ### Current browse context:\nL40: \nL41: math.MG\nL42: \nL43: cite16†< prev |   cite17†next > L44: \nL45: cite18†new | cite19†recent | cite20†2026-08 L46: \nL47: Change to browse by:\nL48: \nL49: cite21†math L50: cite22†math.AP L51: cite23†math.DG L52: \nL53: ### References & Citations\nL54: \nL55:   * cite24†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L56:   * cite25†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L57:   * cite26†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L58: \nL59: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL60: \nL61: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL62: \nL63: [Button: ×]\nL64: \nL65: loading...